@using Fhi.Munin.Explorer.Blazor
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Legacy host — kilder";
}

<div class="hostchrome">
    <p class="hostchrome-note">
        The same MVC mount as the front page, for the package's other root component —
        <code>KildeExplorer</code>, the kildeutforsker. <a href="/">The variable explorer</a> is on
        the front page.
    </p>
</div>

<div class="hostframe">
    @* render-mode is set HERE, by the host. Server rather than ServerPrerendered for the reason
       the front page gives, and for one that applies only to this component: KildeExplorer raises
       SelectedKildeIdChanged, and an EventCallback serialises to an empty delegate across a
       static-SSR boundary. That is what a host wrapper could not survive and this component does
       not have to — the callbacks are created inside it — and it refuses a prerendered mount
       anyway rather than leaving them silently dead.

       VariableExplorerPath is the one thing the package cannot know: where this host mounted the
       other explorer. Everything else that was handed in here — a 103-line wrapper, the request's
       query string and the path this view answers on — is the component's own now
       (Fhi.Metadata-zrcf4). It takes the path from the circuit's address, which already carries
       PathBase, so closing a kilde behind a reverse proxy no longer sends the reader out of the
       application. *@
    <component type="typeof(KildeExplorerWithUrlState)"
               render-mode="Server"
               param-Language="@("no")"
               param-VariableExplorerPath="@("/")" />
</div>
